{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find the element that appears only once in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    \n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        \n        # If mid is even, its pair should be at mid+1\n        # If mid is odd, its pair should be at mid-1\n        if mid % 2 == 0:\n            if arr[mid] == arr[mid + 1]:\n                left = mid + 2\n            else:\n                right = mid\n        else:\n            if arr[mid] == arr[mid - 1]:\n                left = mid + 1\n            else:\n                right = mid\n    \n    return arr[left]"}
