{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sort array using pancake sort algorithm by repeatedly flipping largest element to end.\"\"\"\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return arr\n    \n    result = arr[:]\n    n = len(result)\n    \n    def flip(arr, k):\n        \"\"\"Reverse elements from index 0 to k.\"\"\"\n        arr[:k+1] = arr[:k+1][::-1]\n    \n    def find_max_index(arr, end):\n        \"\"\"Find index of maximum element up to end position.\"\"\"\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, end + 1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n    \n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        max_idx = find_max_index(result, curr_size - 1)\n        \n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                flip(result, max_idx)\n            flip(result, curr_size - 1)\n    \n    return result"}
