{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    # Handle edge cases\n    if not arr or k == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Find max subarray sum in single array using Kadane's algorithm\n    def kadane(array):\n        max_sum = array[0]\n        current_sum = array[0]\n        for i in range(1, len(array)):\n            current_sum = max(array[i], current_sum + array[i])\n            max_sum = max(max_sum, current_sum)\n        return max_sum\n    \n    # If k = 1, return kadane's result\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane(arr)\n    \n    # Create array with 2 repetitions to handle wrap-around cases\n    double_arr = arr + arr\n    max_double = kadane(double_arr)\n    \n    # If k = 2, return result from double array\n    if k == 2:\n        return max_double\n    \n    # For k > 2, consider three cases:\n    # 1. Max subarray is within single array\n    # 2. Max subarray spans exactly 2 arrays\n    # 3. Max subarray spans more than 2 arrays (includes middle complete arrays)\n    \n    single_max = kadane(arr)\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n    \n    # If total sum is positive, we can benefit from repeating middle arrays\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        # Max sum would be: best from double array + (k-2) * total_sum\n        return max(single_max, max_double + (k - 2) * total_sum)\n    else:\n        # If total sum is not positive, best is either single array or double array\n        return max(single_max, max_double)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    \"\"\"Find the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in array repeated k times.\"\"\"\n    if k == 1:\n        max_ending_here = max_so_far = arr[0]\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            max_ending_here = max(arr[i], max_ending_here + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n        return max_so_far\n    \n    # Find max subarray sum for single array\n    max_kadane = max_ending_here = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        max_ending_here = max(arr[i], max_ending_here + arr[i])\n        max_kadane = max(max_kadane, max_ending_here)\n    \n    # Find max prefix and suffix sums\n    curr_sum = 0\n    max_prefix = float('-inf')\n    for i in range(n):\n        curr_sum += arr[i]\n        max_prefix = max(max_prefix, curr_sum)\n    \n    curr_sum = 0\n    max_suffix = float('-inf')\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n        curr_sum += arr[i]\n        max_suffix = max(max_suffix, curr_sum)\n    \n    # Total sum of one array\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n    \n    # Find max subarray sum in two concatenated arrays\n    max_two_arrays = max_ending_here = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, 2*n):\n        max_ending_here = max(arr[i % n], max_ending_here + arr[i % n])\n        max_two_arrays = max(max_two_arrays, max_ending_here)\n    \n    if total_sum <= 0:\n        return max(max_kadane, max_two_arrays)\n    else:\n        return max(max_kadane, max_two_arrays, max_prefix + max_suffix + (k-2) * total_sum)"}
