{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence ending at i, then including element at k\n    dp_i = [0] * (i + 1)\n    dp_i[0] = arr[0]\n    \n    for j in range(1, i + 1):\n        dp_i[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[j]:\n                dp_i[j] = max(dp_i[j], dp_i[prev] + arr[j])\n    \n    max_sum_at_i = max(dp_i)\n    \n    # Add the kth element if it can form an increasing sequence\n    result = max_sum_at_i\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            result = max(result, dp_i[j] + arr[k])\n    \n    return result"}
