{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence ending at index i\n    dp_i = [0] * (i + 1)\n    dp_i[0] = arr[0]\n    \n    for j in range(1, i + 1):\n        dp_i[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[j]:\n                dp_i[j] = max(dp_i[j], dp_i[prev] + arr[j])\n    \n    max_sum_at_i = max(dp_i)\n    \n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence starting from index k\n    dp_k = [0] * (n - k)\n    dp_k[0] = arr[k]\n    \n    for j in range(1, n - k):\n        idx = k + j\n        dp_k[j] = arr[idx]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            prev_idx = k + prev\n            if arr[prev_idx] < arr[idx]:\n                dp_k[j] = max(dp_k[j], dp_k[prev] + arr[idx])\n    \n    max_sum_from_k = max(dp_k)\n    \n    return max_sum_at_i + max_sum_from_k"}
