{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all ludic numbers up to n using the ludic sieve algorithm.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # Take the first number as ludic\n        first = numbers[0]\n        ludic.append(first)\n        \n        # Remove every k-th element where k is the first number\n        if first == 1:\n            numbers = numbers[1:]\n        else:\n            new_numbers = []\n            for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n                if (i + 1) % first != 0:\n                    new_numbers.append(num)\n            numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic"}
