{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the nth Bell number using dynamic programming with Bell triangle.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Create Bell triangle\n    bell = [[0 for i in range(n+1)] for j in range(n+1)]\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        # First element in each row is same as last element of previous row\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i-1][i-1]\n        \n        # Fill the rest of the row\n        for j in range(1, i+1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i-1][j-1] + bell[i][j-1]\n    \n    return bell[n][0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all Ludic numbers less than or equal to n. Ludic numbers are generated by a sieve-like process starting with natural numbers.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # Take the first number as the next Ludic number\n        first = numbers[0]\n        ludic.append(first)\n        \n        # Remove every k-th element where k is the current Ludic number\n        # Skip the first removal since we already took the first element\n        new_numbers = [numbers[0]]  # Keep the first element\n        for i in range(1, len(numbers)):\n            if (i - 0) % first != 0:  # Keep elements that are not at positions divisible by first\n                new_numbers.append(numbers[i])\n        \n        numbers = new_numbers[1:]  # Remove the first element for next iteration\n    \n    return ludic"}
